results/
*.log
batch_evaluation.log

# Data (download from HuggingFace, not committed)
bird-interact-lite/
bird-interact-full/

# Local-only provider override
shared/_local_provider.py
shared/_legacy_*.py

# Local-only run scripts (personal task subsets, local endpoints)
scripts/[0-9]*run.sh
scripts/run_*.sh

# Holds a live Apps Script deployment URL + write token
scripts/sheet.py

# docs/ is DENY BY DEFAULT. Everything in it is ignored unless named below, so a
# new working note, investigation record or handoff is untracked the moment it is
# written and nobody has to remember to add a line here. That is the failure this
# replaces: the old list was opt-out, and three handoff docs plus a build prompt
# whose own commit message said "LOCAL ONLY - do not upstream" were committed
# simply because no line covered them, then rode a share-branch merge (6209b35)
# onto feature/atscale-mcp-semantic-layer.
#
# To share a new doc, add a "!docs/<name>" line here in the same commit. Keep the
# list short and only for things a teammate needs: harness documentation, the
# model change log, durable references and reusable prompts — never a working
# note, a plan, an investigation record or a session handoff.
#
# CAVEAT, because a rule that looks stronger than it is will get trusted too far:
# .gitignore has NO effect on a file git already tracks. Adding a line here does
# not untrack anything — that takes `git rm --cached`, and that deletion reaches a
# teammate's working copy when they next merge, so it is a coordinated move, not a
# tidy-up. Nothing in docs/ is tracked-but-ignored as of 66e0ab2; keep it that way
# by putting a new working note in a NEW file, which this rule ignores on creation.
docs/*
!docs/architecture.png
!docs/architecture.svg
!docs/model-change-log.md
!docs/bird-grading-comparison.md
!docs/bird-database-testing-prompt.md

# Personal / development files
Bird_ADK_plan.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
reference_code_paper/

# Editor scratch
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# offline re-grade row caches (large, regenerable)
.regrade_cache_*.pkl
